{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MIC",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Woe to them that devise iniquity, and work evil upon their beds! when the morning is light, they practice it, because it is in the power of their hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they covet fields, and take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by violence; and houses, and take ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " away: so they oppress a man and his house, even a man and his heritage.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore thus saith the LORD; Behold, against this family do I devise an evil, from which ye shall not remove your necks; neither shall ye go haughtily: for this time ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In that day shall ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " take up a parable against you, and lament with a grievous lamentation, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " say, We are utterly wasted: he hath changed the portion of my people: how hath he removed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from me! turning away he hath divided our fields.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore thou shalt have none that shall cast a cord by lot in the congregation of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Prophesy ye not, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "say they to them that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " prophesy: they shall not prophesy to them, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " they shall not take shame.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thou that art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " named the house of Jacob, is the spirit of the LORD straitened? are these his doings? do not my words do good to him that walketh uprightly?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even of late my people hath risen up as an enemy: ye pull off the robe with the garment from them that pass by securely as men averse to war.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The women of my people have ye cast out from their pleasant houses; from their children have ye taken away my glory for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise ye, and depart; for this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rest: because it is polluted, it shall destroy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "you",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", even with a grievous destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If a man walking in the spirit and falsehood doth lie, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saying",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I will prophesy to thee of wine and of strong drink; he shall even be the prophet of this people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will surely assemble, O Jacob, all of thee; I will surely gather the remnant of Israel; I will put them together as the sheep of Bozrah, as the flock in the midst of their fold: they shall make great noise by reason of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the multitude of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The breaker is come up before them: they have broken up, and have passed through the gate, and have gone out by it; and their king shall pass before them, and the LORD on the head of them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
